In [1] a conjecture for the modular transformation of the free fermion generalised Gibbs ensemble (GGE) was given where only the KdV charge associated to the weight four quasi primary field was inserted. In this paper we first generalise this conjecture to the case with an arbitrary, finite collection of KdV charges in the GGE. These GGEs are generalisations of the generating function of power partitions. We prove the conjectured transformation for the case with a finite number of charges inserted and discuss the case with an infinite number of charges. In [ref] the modular transformation properties of the generalised eta function \(\eta_s(	au)\) , defined by \[\eta_s(	au) = e^{-\pi i \zeta(-s)	au}\prod_{m=1}^\infty \left(1 - e^{2\pi i m^s 	au}ight)\;,\] where \(\zeta(z)\) is the Riemann zeta function, were studied. It was proved that under the modular S transformation, \(	auightarrow-1/	au\) , \(\eta_s\) satisfies \[\eta_s(	au) = (2\pi)^{ rac{s-1}{2}}\sqrt{i/	au} \prod_{\substack{	ext{Im}(z)>0\ 	au z^s = \pm 1}} \eta_{1/s}(z)\;.\] In the above expression the product is taken over the roots of the two polynomials \(	au z^s=\pm 1\) such that the imaginary part of the roots are positive. In this paper we study the modular transformation properties of a further generalisation of the Dedekind eta function where we replace the powers \(m^s\) in the product in [•] with polynomials. For each \(N=2,3,\dots\) we have a generalised eta function \(\eta_{\alpha, eta}(	au,\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_{2N-1})\) defined by \[ egin{split} \eta_{\alpha, eta}(	au,\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_{2N-1}) =& \exp\left(-\pi i \sum_{n=1}^N \alpha_{2n-1} 	au^{2n-1} \zeta(1-2n,1-\alpha) ight) \ &	imes \prod_{\substack{k \in \mathbb{Z}+\alpha\ k>0}}^\infty \left( 1 - e^{2\pi i ( eta+ \sum_{n=1}^N \alpha_{2n-1} (	au k)^{2n-1})} ight)\;, \end{split}\] where \(\zeta(s,a)\) is the Hurwitz zeta function, defined in [•]. The product in [•] converges for Im \((\alpha_{2N-1}	au^{2N-1})>0\) and the Hurwitz zeta function is defined for \(a 
eq 0,-1,\dots\) . While \(\eta_{\alpha, eta}\) can be defined for \(\alpha\in \mathbb{R}\setminus\{1,2,\dots\}\) and \( eta\in \mathbb{R}\) , we will restrict \((\alpha, eta)\) to the four pairs \((0,0)\) , \(\left(0,	frac{1}{2}ight), \left(	frac{1}{2},0ight)\) and \(\left(	frac{1}{2},	frac{1}{2}ight)\) since these functions are related to the Generalised Gibbs ensemble of a free fermion in 2 dimensions as described below. We will additionally assume throughout that Im \((	au)>0\) but place no restriction on the \(\alpha_{2n-1}	au^{2n-1}\) for \(n<N\) . This is not the most general order \(2N-1\) polynomial that one could include in [•], we are restricting to odd polynomials. This restriction is because we will be interested in the link between these generalised eta functions and the generalised Gibbs ensembles studied in [ref] (we will say more about this link below). The only polynomials that occur in these generalised Gibbs ensembles are odd and in addition have a non-vanishing linear term i.e. \(\alpha_1=1\) . Note that we can still relate our results to those of [ref] by setting \(\alpha_{2n-1} = 0\) for \(n<N\) , \(\alpha_{2N-1} = 1\) and \(	au^{2N-1} = 	au'\) , the condition Im \((\alpha_{2N-1}	au^{2N-1}) > 0\) implies Im \((	au') > 0\) . In this paper we will prove the following transformation properties for the generalised eta function [•] \[ egin{split} &\eta_{\alpha, eta}(	au,\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_{2N-1}) = \ &\sqrt{2}^{\delta_{\alpha, rac{1}{2}}\delta_{ eta,0} - \delta_{\alpha,0}\delta_{ eta, rac{1}{2}}} \sqrt{i/	au}^{\delta_{\alpha,0}\delta_{ eta,0}}\exp\left( \int_0^\infty \log(1 - e^{2\pi i eta}e^{2\pi i(\sum_{n=1}^N \alpha_{2n-1} (	au x)^{2n-1})}) dx ight)\ &	imes \prod_{n\in\mathbb{Z}+ eta} \prod_{\substack{z_j(n) \ 	ext{Im}(z_j(n))>0}} (1-e^{2\pi i (\alpha+ z_j(n))})\;, \end{split}\] where the \(z_j(x)\) , \(j=1,\dots,2N-1\) are the roots of the polynomial \[\sum_{n=1}^N \alpha_{2n-1} (	au z)^{2n-1} = x\;.\] This transformation formula is valid