eq0\) and Im \((\alpha_{2N-1}	au^{2N-1})\) . For the special case \(\alpha_{2n-1} = 0\) for all \(n<M\leq N\) and \(\alpha_{2M-1} 
eq 0\) the transformation can be found by starting with [•] with \(\alpha_1
